ROUND 2 — reviewed main..cea2c83 (same invocation). P1 fixed in be52680 (operator-approved gate change, Daniel 2026-10-08).
==============================================================================
### Finding

- **P1 — already-inherited failures are still propagated as green evidence.** The inheritance loop skips entries unless they are `captured`/`attached` and retain an `output_file` ([bin/coverloop:1241](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1241)); therefore an already-inherited `self-attested` entry with `status: pass` and non-zero `exit_code` never reaches the correction at [bin/coverloop:1257](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1257). `attest` saves it under the new HEAD, and the default gate accepts its pass status. A disposable-repo reproduction produced: `attest_exit=0, status=pass, exit_code=7, gate_exit=0`. I consider this P1 for this release—not merely the generic gate limitation—because v2.12.2 actively re-inherits the known-failed entry as green evidence. The new inheritance test covers only the first transition from invalid `captured` to `self-attested` ([tests/test_gate.py:1306](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/tests/test_gate.py:1306)), not a subsequent inheritance of that legacy self-attested shape.

  The Upgrading paragraph correctly admits that these reports remain green ([CHANGELOG.md:27](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/CHANGELOG.md:27)), but “re-attest those commits” is insufficient unless it specifically means rerunning/replacing the affected evidence record; a normal `attest --tests` preserves the problem. Its grep finds affected reports but also overmatches rejected captured failures. The unconditional “stays fail” statement in [docs/GATE.md:65](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/docs/GATE.md:65) is therefore inaccurate for this acknowledged legacy shape.

Everything else checked out: new captures behave correctly for codex/GLM/mutation, successful pass captures remain pass, mutation guard counts survive, attached entries remain unaffected, report-shape validation accepts the new records, and the three gate functions named in the changelog are untouched. The three targeted tests passed; the full suite passed all 251 tests; `git diff --check` passed.

