ROUND 3 — reviewed main..be52680 (same invocation; operator-approved third round past the 2-round cap). P2 #2 (CHANGELOG wording) fixed in db56a13, a CHANGELOG-only commit not re-reviewed. P2 #1 (exit_code shape validation, pre-existing) deferred as a follow-up.
==============================================================================
- **P2 — `exit_code` lacks shape validation.** [`bin/coverloop:735`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:735) validates other nested fields but not `exit_code`. Consequently, `false`, `null`, and `0.0` can gate as successful; `false` also passes captured evidence under `--require-executed` because [`verify_capture`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1526) treats it as integer zero. Require an actual non-boolean integer whenever the field is present. New tests only cover integer `0/1/7` at [`tests/test_gate.py:1287`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/tests/test_gate.py:1287), leaving this unpinned. The withheld-placeholder guard still prevents this from laundering a genuine failed capture, so this is not P1.

- **P2 — Upgrading guidance overstates the affected set.** [`CHANGELOG.md:33`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/CHANGELOG.md:33) says matching reports “now fail,” and its grep matches non-zero GLM records too, although GLM remains advisory by [`bin/coverloop:1671`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1671). It should disclose that false positive. The suggested `attest --<record>-run`/`--<record>-log` shorthand is also incomplete: a verdict plus command/file is mandatory at [`bin/coverloop:1372`](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1372).

The intended integer behavior for (a), (b), and (c) is correctly implemented. Negative exit codes fail, successful/inherited evidence remains accepted, mutation guard counts survive, and GLM remains advisory. Full suite: **253/253 passed**; `git diff --check` passed; worktree remained clean.

VERDICT: PASS (no open P0/P1)
